    every result; ``total`` is the number of items and ``valid`` is
    the number of those rows whose ``rank`` is not ``None``, with
    ``coverage = valid / total``.  When ``valid < minimum``, ``mean``,
    ``std``, ``uncertainty`` and ``rank`` are all ``None``; otherwise
    ``mean`` is the mean of the rows' ``mean`` values, ``std`` is the
    population standard deviation of those values and
    ``uncertainty`` is the ``hypot`` of every valid row's
    ``uncertainty`` divided by ``valid``.

